This implementation:

Preserves the exact C++ algorithm - all transformations and calculations match
Handles file I/O correctly - reads the C++ format files
Provides CPU reference - for validation against C++ results
GPU acceleration - uses wgpu compute shaders
No silent failures - explicit error handling everywhere
Clear data flow - from problem definition to GPU buffers

Key design decisions:

Used f64 for CPU to match C++ precision exactly
Used f32 for GPU (standard for GPU compute)
Flattened arrays for GPU memory efficiency
Explicit padding in structs for alignment
Workgroup size of 64 (tunable based on GPU)

The main challenge was the rotation matrix storage order difference between C++ and the file format - I've handled this in the file loader.
